---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Use — ExactSize"
  description="Terms for using ExactSize's browser-based image tools and source-linked requirement guides."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">Last updated: 27 October 2026. By using ExactSize, you agree to these terms.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content">
    <section class="prose">
      <h2>What ExactSize provides</h2>
      <p>ExactSize provides browser-based image tools and informational guides for selected application and photo requirements. The site is an independent project, not an official government, passport, visa, exam-board, or application service.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Information is not an approval</h2>
      <p>Guides summarize requirements from linked sources as of their displayed verification dates. Requirements can change and may depend on your exact application path. Check the current instructions from the organization receiving your file before relying on a measurement or preset.</p>
      <p>Tool results are provided for convenience and are not legal, immigration, exam, or professional advice. A result that matches a displayed file size or pixel check does not guarantee that an authority will accept the image or application.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Your files and downloads</h2>
      <p>Image compression and resizing run in your browser on your device. The passport-photo preflight performs limited metadata checks and does not modify the selected photo. ExactSize does not upload your image files. You are responsible for choosing the right requirements, reviewing the result, and keeping any original or downloaded files you need.</p>
      <p>Only use images that you have permission to use. Do not rely on the site for emergency or time-critical decisions.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>Tools and guides may be changed, interrupted, or removed. ExactSize is provided without a promise of uninterrupted availability or error-free results. To the extent permitted by applicable law, the site is provided “as is”; nothing in these terms limits rights that cannot legally be limited.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:periscopebookeeping@gmail.com">periscopebookeeping@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
